          "guid": "mt3f5h18axwd9tj4",
          "message": {
            "text": "Affine matrix3d scale/translation must follow the same live-baked route as matrix scale/translation. The previous blanket matrix3d freeze was asymmetric with threadFrozenTransform, which serializes only planar rotation/skew: a pure matrix3d scale was removed during capture and never re-emitted. Non-affine matrix3d remains safely owned by transformSubtreeRaster; the DPR source-crop E2E uses an affine matrix3d specifically to guard this boundary.",
            "markdown": "Affine matrix3d scale/translation must follow the same live-baked route as matrix scale/translation. The previous blanket matrix3d freeze was asymmetric with threadFrozenTransform, which serializes only planar rotation/skew: a pure matrix3d scale was removed during capture and never re-emitted. Non-affine matrix3d remains safely owned by transformSubtreeRaster; the DPR source-crop E2E uses an affine matrix3d specifically to guard this boundary."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/script/walker/transforms.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 206,
                  "endLine": 219,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    // Heuristic: do we need to clear inlines to capture an un-rotated layout\n    // box? Pure translate/scale leaves the layout box axis-aligned so we\n    // keep the live-rect model. Anything containing a rotate(...) or skew\n    // function — including the freshly composed string — needs the freeze.\n    // DM-2380: matrix3d() is not itself a reason to freeze. Its planar b/c\n    // terms use the same test as matrix(); an affine matrix3d scale/translate\n    // stays live and is baked once, while a genuinely projective context is\n    // owned by transformSubtreeRaster. Freezing every matrix3d but serializing\n    // only rotation/skew dropped affine scale before the replaced snapshot was\n    // emitted.\n    const needsFreeze =\n      transformHasRotationOrSkew(originalTransform) ||\n      /\\brotate\\b/.test(originalTransform) ||\n      /\\bskew/.test(originalTransform);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
